description.narrative:
This programme aims to contribute to a reduction in urban poverty and the impact of climate change through securing sustainable living conditions for poor and disadvantaged families living in slums, derelict tenements, illegal settlements and on the streets of the city of Sao Paulo. The livelihoods focus is on promoting access to housing and basic services. The CC focus is on advocating for mitigation and adaptation policies. 

This programme is projected to begin fully in September 2011 but the initial stage of this programme, a Climate Change seminar will be held in Sao Paulo, Brazil from 25-27th November 2010, jointly organised with Christian Aid. Speakers will include both CAFOD and Christian Aid partners, and key representatives from government and civil society organisations. 

The three main objectives of the seminar will be: 
1.To build understanding amongst excluded people living in Sao Paulo about the impact of CC, and support the inclusion of a CC agenda amongst social movements and organisations;
2.To contribute to the CC debate and generate future training materials; 
3. To strengthen networks and capacity regarding CC.
